From: (to be filled by the sender)
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v2: alias kv_b_proj on attn_mha without registering a submodule

Refresh of sgl-project/sglang#35715 (youssef62) against origin/main: since 2d8484740d (#35314)
the forward_prepare fill-in carries an `and hasattr(self, "kv_b_proj")` guard, so the
open PR no longer applies as written. Fixes #35702 (auto-closed as inactive, still present).

---
--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/deepseek_v2.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/deepseek_v2.py
@@ -2290,7 +2290,9 @@
             init_modelslim_mla_kv(self, prefix)
 
         self.alt_stream = alt_stream
-        self.attn_mha.kv_b_proj = None
+        # Alias for backends that only get the RadixAttention layer. Not registered
+        # as a submodule: a second state_dict name breaks sharded_state round-trips.
+        object.__setattr__(self.attn_mha, "kv_b_proj", self.kv_b_proj)
 
         self.w_kc = None
         self.w_vc = None
@@ -2459,9 +2461,6 @@
         llama_4_scaling: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,
         prev_topk_indices: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,
     ):
-        if self.attn_mha.kv_b_proj is None and hasattr(self, "kv_b_proj"):
-            self.attn_mha.kv_b_proj = self.kv_b_proj
-
         # when hidden_states is a tuple of tensors, the tuple will include quantized weight and scale tensor
         if isinstance(hidden_states, tuple):
             if (
